---
/**
 * P7 Employers: /partner-with-us/employers/ (T3, implements doc 04 matrix 4.6).
 * C1 to C14 in order, as the numbered table in doc 06 P7, without C3 (Cost of Waiting) and C4 (Imagine), which the audience pages leave to Home since WP47.
 * WP30c (owner direction 2026-10-14, "less is more"): every CMF band stays, each states its point once. Gone: the In Short summary, the fit check, the second statement of the
 * placement-team sentence (the hiring band says it), the restated "measures you set" card and the fifth next step. Three FAQs, not five.
 * WP31 (cycle-8 review): the youth programs' trial, survey and paid-work pathway blocks are gone from this corporate offer page; "Broader Evidence from Our Youth Programs" is a two-link
 * group to the evidence pages (no figure from the youth programs is shown here).
 * WP32 (cycle-9 review): the employer credentials (Grameenphone Academy enrollments, AWS Authorized Training Partner, AIvolve) are stated once, in "Our Track Record"; the delivery-record cards that repeated them are gone.
 * WP36 (cycle-13 review): the three pains are statements; the closing reassurance read "Your first step is a conversation, not a commitment." (the first step may be a hiring request); WP129 (Opus High run 4): it reads "A discovery session is a conversation, not a commitment.", as on every other page, because the first step is a discovery session on both routes.
 * WP39 (cycle-16 review): "What Your Business Gets" is three short cards (IncludesBand), not the concern / inclusion / benefit matrix.
 * WP41 (cycle-18 review): "Our Track Record" leads with its delivered figure (the 23,000+ Grameenphone Academy enrollments, as the headline stat); the ministry contract keeps its "Contract scope:" wording (the register's
 * presentation rule: a scope of work is never worded as delivered training), the AIvolve partnership is the one other line, and "AWS Authorized Training Partner" is a line under the logo strip, beside the AWS logo.
 * "AI Is Reshaping the Workforce" states the 11M and 9M jobs and leaves the all-trends clause out.
 * WP47 (owner decision 2026-10-15): the page opens with its own proof and goes straight to its offer. The Cost of Waiting band ("AI Is Changing the Skills Your Teams Need": the 11M and 9M jobs, the AI-skills growth) and the Imagine
 * band ("What Changes for Your Team") are gone; Home carries them. Nothing on this page depended on them: the 72% hiring gap stays in the problem band, and the
 * AI-workflow and certification claims are in "JobReady@Work: Built Around Your Roles" and "What Your Business Gets". The hiring route's two steps are the shared EMPLOYER_HIRING_STEPS (JobReady@Work uses them too).
 * WP50 (cycle-25 review): the pricing sentence ("Pricing is set per program; we share an indicative budget in the discovery session and confirm it after the needs assessment.") is said once, in the "What Does It Cost?" answer (Q8-employer);
 * "Choose How to Work with Us" no longer repeats it as its lead, so the band has none (the EMPLOYER_PRICING constant is gone from copy.ts with its last two readers).
 * WP54 (cycle-28 reviews, Kimi K2, K3 and K5): the closing strip under "What Happens Next" is the first-action line alone ("Your first step, for team training or hiring: a discovery session. In your inquiry, include two suitable times."): the
 * "Private-sector partners include Grameenphone Academy, Robi, Accenture, BASIS and AWS." line is gone, because the Track Record band's logo strip names the same organizations (as on Development Partners, Governments, Universities and Foundations);
 * "AWS Authorized Training Partner" is a sentence of that strip's caption ("... not endorsements. CodersTrust is an AWS Authorized Training Partner."), not a lone paragraph under the logos.
 * WP57 (cycle-29 review, GPT-6.1 Sol G7): "Due Diligence in One View" is three rows (contracting entities, needs assessment, progress evaluation); its "Independent Evaluation Welcome" row is gone, because "Broader Evidence from Our Youth Programs" links the trial
 * and the pilot-team band after it (RiskReversalBand) has the same item.
 * WP66 (owner request 2026-10-20): the Track Record band's list closes with the signed-agreement sentence for companies and industry bodies (SC-11d, `signed` on PartnerGuideBand: "CodersTrust has signed MOUs, agreements or contracts with ... companies and industry bodies."),
 * after the contract line; the band's heading says "Since 2014", so the sentence leaves the year to it.
 * WP104 (owner answer 2026-10-29: the AIvolve agreement is an MOU only): the AIvolve line (PA-07) is no longer in this band, which is a track record of delivery; JobReady@Work names AIvolve as an offering in its Training row.
 * WP175 (owner decisions of 28 November 2026: every conversion page follows CMF v3, C1 to C14, in order and coverage; tests/wp175-employers.spec.ts): every band sits in a Tone wrapper (data-cmf). The "Your
 * Next Step" routes and the "See the Program" link move under the definition, so GEO directly follows the hero. C2–C4 is a declared compression: the pains are EMPLOYER_PAINS (the same words, now P1 to P3,
 * data-pain) and the band ends with the C3 transition line (C3_TRANSITION). C5 opens with the empathy line (EMPATHY.employers, a fresh line: not the one WP61 retired) and ends with JobReady@Work's method line
 * (METHOD.employers: each program is built around a needs assessment, IN-10); C6 no longer prints the TalentLEAP line or its link (WP166-B R3-29 had put them there; WP161 A-37: JobReady@Work is not the TalentLEAP
 * path), so the method is said once. C6 is the light mechanism band (HomeMechanism, airy), because the C7 trial band (ProofBand, Klein) now follows it and two dark bands never touch (tests/wp47.spec.ts). C7 is the
 * trial band again (WP31, a cycle-8 review, had made it two links): the one-line trial lead (TRIAL_LEAD), the TRIAL-SCOPE line directly under it (TRIAL_SCOPE.work, doc 04 4.6 and doc 06 P7), the survey sentence with
 * its bold "From CodersTrust’s youth programs:" lead-in (S4-M5), the two evidence links; then Mysha's story (it stood before the problem band, WP24a). C8 is EMPLOYER_INCLUDES (P1 to P3: the customized curriculum now
 * answers "Hiring alone does not close the gap" and the AI-skills card the AI wage premium) and "How It Works in Three Steps" (EMPLOYER_STEPS, with step 2 as `employerSteps` below); doc 04 4.6 and doc 06 P7 name no
 * gain creator, so none is drafted. The due-diligence view joins C9; C10 is the short "What Makes CodersTrust Different" band: USP 3 in its employer form and USP 1, the independent evidence (doc 04 4.6 names USPs 3
 * and 4, but USP 4's line is about labs, colleges and Training of Trainers, which describe youth delivery, not employer team training, and a page that explains delivery must name its facilitators, tests/wp152.spec.ts);
 * the hiring band joins C11, before the options.
 */
import LearnerVoice from '../../../components/pages/impact/LearnerVoice.astro';
import LandingLayout from '../../../layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import HeroBand from '../../../components/sections/HeroBand.astro';
import ProblemBand from '../../../components/sections/ProblemBand.astro';
import IncludesBand from '../../../components/sections/IncludesBand.astro';
import FAQBand from '../../../components/sections/FAQBand.astro';
import RiskReversalBand from '../../../components/sections/RiskReversalBand.astro';
import ProofBand from '../../../components/sections/ProofBand.astro';
import DifferenceBand from '../../../components/sections/DifferenceBand.astro';
import DueDiligenceView from '../../../components/pages/hub/DueDiligenceView.astro';
import HomeMechanism from '../../../components/pages/home/HomeMechanism.astro';
import Tone from '../../../components/pages/home/Tone.astro';
import Section from '../../../components/ui/Section.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../../../components/ui/SectionHeader.astro';
import Icon from '../../../components/system/Icon.astro';
import GainsPains from '../../../components/pages/partners/GainsPains.astro';
import HowItWorks from '../../../components/pages/partners/HowItWorks.astro';
import PartnerGuideBand from '../../../components/pages/partners/PartnerGuideBand.astro';
import SubBand from '../../../components/pages/partners/SubBand.astro';
import Callout from '../../../components/pages/partners/Callout.astro';
import RouteLink from '../../../components/pages/partners/RouteLink.astro';
import OfferCards from '../../../components/pages/partners/OfferCards.astro';
import DualCtaBand from '../../../components/pages/partners/DualCtaBand.astro';
import StepsBand from '../../../components/pages/partners/StepsBand.astro';
import RouteBlock from '../../../components/ui/RouteBlock.astro';
import StepFlow from '../../../components/ui/StepFlow.astro';
import Reinforcement from '../../../components/pages/partners/Reinforcement.astro';
import PageEnhancements from '../../../components/pages/partners/PageEnhancements.astro';
import { LINKS, meta } from '../../../components/pages/partners/partners';
import { AKIJ_ASSET, AKIJ_STORY, C14, C3_TRANSITION, DELIVERY_MODEL_WORK, EMPATHY, EMPLOYER_HIRING_STEPS, EMPLOYER_INCLUDES, EMPLOYER_PAINS, EMPLOYER_STEPS, HEADLINE, METHOD, MICRO_COMMITMENT, POSITIONING, PROGRAM_SCOPE_INCLUSIONS, TRACK_MENU_LIST, TRIAL_BAND_HEADING, TRIAL_LEAD, TRIAL_SCOPE, VALUE_PROPOSITION, originShortUnder, painForList } from '../../../data/copy';
import DefinitionPlus from '../../../components/pages/about/DefinitionPlus.astro';
import { contractScope } from '../../../components/sections/copyText';
import { fact } from '../../../data/facts';
import { faqJsonLd } from '../../../lib/faq';
import { cta } from '../../../lib/mailto';
import { webPage } from '../../../lib/schema';
import { linkAttrs } from '../../../lib/url';

const PATH = '/partner-with-us/employers/';
// WP161-A (adversarial review A-02, A-28): the WebPage carries the page's own dateModified (it fell back to the build date); the Hire Talent lead gains register SC-03's "Most delivery has been in Bangladesh." (2026-11-03). WP166-B: 2026-11-21 (the marketing review R3 changes). WP168-B: 2026-11-24 (the Akij Group line leads the track record).
const primary = cta('work');
const talent = cta('talent');

const { title, description } = meta(
  'Corporate AI Training and Digital Talent',
  'Upskill teams for AI and digital work, and hire job-ready digital talent through CodersTrust’s employer training and placement support.',
);

// Q8-employer: the employer pricing answer (the same variant JobReady@Work uses), not the youth-cohort pricing answer.
// WP166-B (marketing review R3-33): the platform question (Q11) is gone; "See the Platform Capabilities" closes "What Your Business Gets" instead.
const FAQ_IDS = ['Q1-employer', 'Q8-employer'];
// WP166-B (R3-06): the track-record heading no longer says "Since 2014", so the signed-agreement sentence carries the year (WP66, signedWith) and the origin line is the year-less form it printed under the old heading ("From a Copenhagen launch to
// work in 16 countries and territories."): "since 2014" is said once in the band (WP64).
const employersOrigin = originShortUnder('We’ve Built This Path Since 2014');
// WP166-B (R3-30): the third obstacle is PX-08 with its source note, as on Investors. WP175: the three pains are EMPLOYER_PAINS (src/data/copy.ts), the same words, shared with JobReady@Work.
// WP175 (C8d): EMPLOYER_STEPS, with step 2 cut to its first clause. WP175-Z: the shared step now says the preparation in WP145's words ("can be added where a track offers one"), the words of this page's
// "Deliver" card in C6 ("Soft-skills and hard-skills tracks; preparation for an industry certification can be added where a track offers one."), and C10 says it again, so the step says the training alone rather
// than repeat the card's clause two bands later. The build stops if the shared step changes, so this cut is revisited then.
const STEP2_PREP = '; preparation for an industry certification can be added where a track offers one.';
if (!EMPLOYER_STEPS[1].text.endsWith(STEP2_PREP)) throw new Error('Employers: EMPLOYER_STEPS step 2 changed; review the page-local cut (employerSteps)');
const employerSteps = [EMPLOYER_STEPS[0], { title: EMPLOYER_STEPS[1].title, text: `${EMPLOYER_STEPS[1].text.slice(0, -STEP2_PREP.length)}.` }, EMPLOYER_STEPS[2]];
// WP46 (cycle-22 review): the hiring route is two steps in the same step component as the training route (it was one sentence beside four steps), both in wording this page already has (EMPLOYER_HIRING_STEPS in copy.ts;
// WP47: JobReady@Work uses the same two steps).
// WP54 (cycle-28 review, Kimi K3): the AWS credential (PA-06, "AWS Authorized Training Partner") is one more sentence of the Track Record logo strip's caption. The sentence is built from the register's words, and the build stops if PA-06 changes.
const aws = fact('PA-06').text;
if (aws !== 'AWS Authorized Training Partner') throw new Error('Employers: PA-06 no longer reads "AWS Authorized Training Partner"; update the caption note');
---

<LandingLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={PATH}
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Partner with Us', href: LINKS.hub }, { label: 'Employers' }]}
  jsonLd={[webPage({ path: PATH, name: title, description, dateModified: '2026-11-28' /* WP175 (owner decisions of 2026-11-28): the crafted C6 statement (Q5), and the CMF v3 bands (the transition line, the C5 empathy and method lines, the trial band with its TRIAL-SCOPE line, the three steps, the short C10) */ }), faqJsonLd('employers', PATH, FAQ_IDS)]}
  stickyCta={{ label: primary.label, href: primary.href }}
>
  <!-- C1 · Identity hook -->
  <Tone cmf="C1">
    <HeroBand
      audience="For Employers"
      title={HEADLINE.employers}
      lead={VALUE_PROPOSITION.employers}
      leadFacts={['IN-10', 'IN-04']}
      cta={{ label: primary.label, href: primary.href }}
      artSeed="partners-employers"
    />
  </Tone>
  <!-- GEO · What is CodersTrust? WP166-B (marketing review R3-34): the definition is followed by the bridge to this reader, as on Investors and Local Partners (JobReady@Work, IN-10).
       WP175: the two routes, one per need (WP24a), and the "See the Program" link (WP20b) sit under the definition, so GEO directly follows the hero. -->
  <Tone cmf="GEO">
    <DefinitionPlus id="definition">
      <p data-fact="IN-10 IN-04">JobReady@Work is its program for employers: training built around your roles and job-ready talent through the placement team.</p>
    </DefinitionPlus>
    <SubBand>
      <Callout eyebrow="Your Next Step">
        <p class="cluster">
          <span>Need training? <a class="link" href="#train-your-team">Train Your Team<Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} /></a></span>
          <span>Need talent? <a class="link" href="#hire-talent">Hire Talent<Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} /></a></span>
        </p>
      </Callout>
    </SubBand>
    <RouteLink kicker="See the Program" label="See the Training Delivery Details" href={LINKS.work} />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C2–C4, declared compressed (WP47, owner decision 2026-10-15, recast 2026-11-28): the three ranked pains (EMPLOYER_PAINS; WP46, WP60 and WP166-B R3-30 wrote them), then the C3 transition line. -->
  <Tone cmf="C2-C4 (compressed)">
    <ProblemBand
      title="The Talent You Need Is Hard to Find"
      bluf="Your roles need digital skills, and your teams need AI skills now."
      factIds={['PX-05']}
      transition={C3_TRANSITION}
    >
      <GainsPains slot="lead" pains={EMPLOYER_PAINS.map(painForList)} />
    </ProblemBand>
  </Tone>

  <!-- C5 · Guide: empathy → ORIGIN → authority → method (WP175, Q2 (a)).
       WP166-B (marketing review R3-06): headed "Employers and Partners We Work With" (the JobReady@Work heading; "We’ve Built This Path Since 2014" is the youth-program heading), the AWS credential (PA-06) is a bullet, not the third sentence
       of the logo caption. WP168-B (owner decision 2026-11-24: Akij Group may be named as a client; marketing review R6, the Akij item): the corporate training for Akij Group (PA-12) is the first item, with a link to the 2023 news post.
       WP175: the band closes with JobReady@Work's method line (METHOD.employers, IN-10). -->
  <Tone cmf="C5">
    <PartnerGuideBand
      title="Employers and Partners We Work With"
      empathy={EMPATHY.employers}
      opening={{ facts: employersOrigin.facts, text: employersOrigin.text }}
      stats={['SC-15']}
      statSize="lg"
      statements={[{ facts: ['PA-12'], link: AKIJ_STORY, asset: AKIJ_ASSET }, { facts: ['PA-06'], text: `${aws}.` }, { facts: ['GV-06'], text: contractScope('GV-06') }]}
      signed="SC-11d"
      partnerGroup="private"
      method={METHOD.employers}
      methodLast
    />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C6 · Mechanism (JobReady@Work), the light variant of the mechanism band (WP175: the C7 trial band after it is the Klein one). WP166-B (marketing review R3-24): the approach closes with the page's one delivery-model sentence
       (DELIVERY_MODEL_WORK). WP175: no TalentLEAP line or link here any more; the method is said once, in C5. -->
  <Tone cmf="C6">
    <HomeMechanism
      tone="airy"
      title="JobReady@Work: Built Around Your Roles"
      positioning={POSITIONING.employers}
      lead={DELIVERY_MODEL_WORK.text}
      blocks={[
        { label: 'Assess', title: 'Needs Assessment', text: 'Scopes the skills and the team size before anything is built.', icon: 'search' },
        { label: 'Design', title: 'Customized Solution and Curriculum', text: 'A curriculum built from your roles, tasks and required tools.', icon: 'pen' },
        { label: 'Deliver', title: 'Interactive Workshops', text: 'Soft-skills and hard-skills tracks; preparation for an industry certification can be added where a track offers one.', icon: 'users' },
        { label: 'Measure', title: 'Progress Evaluation and Support', text: 'Post-training support and a progress evaluation, so outcomes are measurable.', icon: 'chart-bar' },
      ]}
      link={{ label: 'About JobReady@Work', href: LINKS.work }}
    />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C7 · Proof (WP175, Q3 (a); doc 04 4.6 and doc 06 P7: [RCT] with the [TRIAL-SCOPE] line): the trial band again, in its short form. It leads with the one-line trial lead, the relevance line sits directly under it (the trial evaluated
       WSDFM, not JobReady@Work), and the survey sentence says whose survey it is ("From CodersTrust’s youth programs:", S4-M5); no figure claims an employer-training result. WP31 (cycle-8 review) had made the band two links.
       The employer credentials stay in the track-record band above (WP32). Mysha's story follows (it stood before the problem band, WP24a). -->
  <Tone cmf="C7">
    <ProofBand
      title={TRIAL_BAND_HEADING}
      headlineFact="RC-01"
      trialLead={TRIAL_LEAD}
      trialScope={TRIAL_SCOPE.work.text}
      surveyLeadIn="From CodersTrust’s youth programs:"
      statIds={[]}
      compact
      links={[
        { label: 'The Randomized Trial', href: LINKS.trial },
        { label: 'Impact Survey 2026', href: LINKS.outcomes },
      ]}
    />
    <LearnerVoice story="mysha-k-diya" excerpt="A paying job after only two months of Digital Accounting training is a huge accomplishment for me, made possible by the mentorship of CodersTrust." program="Digital Accounting course, CodersTrust Bangladesh" tone="white" />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C8 · Features to benefits. WP39 (cycle-16 review): three short cards in place of the concern / inclusion / benefit matrix. WP175: the cards are EMPLOYER_INCLUDES, in the order of the three pains in C2 (P1 job-ready candidates; P2 the
       customized curriculum, since hiring alone does not close the gap; P3 the AI-skills card, for the AI wage premium), each with its painId; then "How It Works in Three Steps" (EMPLOYER_STEPS). Doc 04 4.6 and doc 06 P7 name no gain
       creator for this page, so none is drafted. WP166-B (marketing review R3-33): "See the Platform Capabilities" closes the band. -->
  <Tone cmf="C8">
    <IncludesBand
      title="What Your Business Gets"
      cards={EMPLOYER_INCLUDES}
      scope={PROGRAM_SCOPE_INCLUSIONS}
    >
      <a slot="more" class="link" href={linkAttrs(LINKS.platform).href}>See the Platform Capabilities<Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} /></a>
    </IncludesBand>
    <HowItWorks steps={employerSteps} />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C9 · Objections, then the compact due-diligence view (WP166-B R3-32: it keeps its contracting card and its "Ask About Due Diligence" link; every audience page keeps its own due-diligence block, tests/wp30c.spec.ts). WP175: it sat after the offer. -->
  <Tone cmf="C9">
    <FAQBand
      audience="employers"
      ids={FAQ_IDS}
      title="Questions Employers Ask"
    />
    <DueDiligenceView compact audience="employers" id="due-diligence" />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C10 · Differentiation (WP175): the short band, USP 3 in its employer form (certification preparation where a track offers one) and USP 1 (independent evidence on CodersTrust's own training); doc 04 4.6's USP 4 (labs,
       colleges, Training of Trainers) describes youth delivery, not team training (see the note at the top). The full comparison table stays off this page (WP47). -->
  <Tone cmf="C10">
    <DifferenceBand usps={['credentialWork', 'evidence']} />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C11 · Offer: the hiring route (WP175: it sat before the problem band, WP20b) and the two in-page routes (Train Your Team, Hire Talent) -->
  <Tone cmf="C11">
    <Section id="hire-talent" tone="airy" pad="sm" aria-labelledby="hire-h">
      <!-- WP166-B (marketing review R3-07): the lead names the tracks candidates come from (PD-10's menu, TRACK_MENU_LIST); "Most delivery has been in Bangladesh." (A-28) stays where the reviewer asked the owner for where candidates are based. -->
      <SectionHeader id="hire-h" eyebrow="Hire Talent" title="Job-Ready Talent Through the Placement Team" lead={`Our placement team introduces job-ready candidates from tracks such as ${TRACK_MENU_LIST}. Most delivery has been in Bangladesh. Talent requests are scoped against the experience and credentials available in the candidate pool.`} />
      <p data-fact="IN-04 PD-10 SC-03"><a class="link" href={talent.href}>{talent.label}<Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} /></a></p>
    </Section>
    <OfferCards
      title="Choose How to Work with Us"
      cards={[
        // WP166-B (marketing review R3-31): each option carries its own inquiry link (the same prefilled emails as the closing band's two actions).
        { id: 'train-your-team', eyebrow: 'Option 1', title: 'A Training Program Scoped to Your Team', text: 'Custom curriculum and interactive workshops, built from a needs assessment of your roles.', facts: ['IN-10'], action: { label: primary.label, href: primary.href } },
        { eyebrow: 'Option 2', title: 'Talent Through the Placement Team', text: 'Access to job-ready candidates introduced through CodersTrust’s placement team.', facts: ['IN-04'], action: { label: talent.label, href: talent.href } },
      ]}
    />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C12 · Risk reversal (immediately before C13). WP166-B (marketing review R3-32): the pilot band's "Independent Evaluation Welcome" card (a funder concept) is gone. -->
  <Tone cmf="C12">
    <RiskReversalBand
      title="Start with a Pilot Team, Then Decide on Evidence"
      lead="Success measures cover completion, any certification the track offers and the role-specific skills you prioritize."
      points={[
        { icon: 'rocket', title: 'Pilot Team First', text: 'Start with one team and see what changes.' },
        { icon: 'handshake', title: 'Scaling Up Is Your Decision', text: 'You choose whether and how far to scale.' },
      ]}
    />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C13 · Call to action: one solid primary, one outline -->
  <Tone cmf="C13">
    <DualCtaBand
      id="cta"
      heading="Let’s Plan Your First Team Program"
      primary={{ label: primary.label, href: primary.href }}
      secondary={{ label: talent.label, href: talent.href }}
      micro={MICRO_COMMITMENT}
    />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C14 · Next steps. WP34 (cycle-11 review): the offer is training and hiring, so the steps are labeled "For Team Training" and hiring has its own short route; the "Hire JobReady Talent" link stays in the C13 band above. -->
  <Tone cmf="C14">
    <StepsBand
      route="For Team Training"
      steps={[
        { title: 'Discovery Session', text: 'A conversation about your roles, team size and timeline.' },
        { title: 'Needs Assessment', text: 'We scope the skills your roles need.' },
        { title: 'Agreement', text: 'Scope, schedule and success measures are agreed.' },
        { title: 'First Workshop or Cohort', text: 'Training starts with your pilot team, and results are checked against the measures you set.' },
      ]}
    >
      <RouteBlock label="For Hiring">
        <div data-fact="IN-04"><StepFlow level={4} steps={EMPLOYER_HIRING_STEPS} /></div>
      </RouteBlock>
    </StepsBand>
    <Reinforcement firstAction={C14.variants.employers} logos={false} reminder={false} />
  </Tone>

  <PageEnhancements />
</LandingLayout>

